        "text": "Subsecciones de: Chapter 9 Connecting to the Internet\nP\u00e1ginas: 169-188\n\u2022 Internet Connectivity 101  (169)\n\u2022 Setting Up the Hardware  (171)\n\u2022 Selecting an Internet Service Provider (ISP)  (172)\n\u2022 Getting Information You Need from Your ISP  (173)\n\u2022 Configuring Your Connection  (174)\n  \u2022 Network Manager  (174)\n  \u2022 Command line tools  (179)\n  \u2022 Dialin\u2019 out  (185)\n\u2022 It\u2019s All Fun and Games Until Something Doesn\u2019t Work  (185)\n\u2022 After You\u2019re Connected  (187)\nChapter 9\nConnecting to the\nInternet\nY\nou may already be connected to the Internet if you\u2019re on a machine that\u2019s\nconnected to a LAN, and you\u2019ve configured the networking during installa-\ntion. To test whether you have a connection, open a web browser and try to\ngo to an outside website (such as www.gnu.org ). If it works, you\u2019re up! No need for\nthis chapter. Otherwise, read on.",
